    "created_at": "2016-07-14T15:10:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-14T15:10:52Z",
    "body": "Right, if we actually change the order of things in the algorithm, it behave different.  I think we need to give devs an algorithm that is easiest to reason about without regard for the effeciency of the spec'ed algorithm, and then implementor can optimize.  Also, we could put a non-normative note to indicate to implementors that there is an opportunity to optimize. \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
