    "updated_at": "2016-07-14T17:08:28Z",
    "body": "Yeah... Meditated on this a bit... Thought of video and photo editing tools that I've used. It seems it is the convention to crop (or mask) in pre-tranform space (local layer space).  I think it is probably the more natural way to reason about cropping. We probably should flip it around...  I think providing a diagram similar to the one we have for drawImage would be useful.\n",
