    "updated_at": "2018-02-28T16:43:17Z",
    "body": "Here's what I was on about.\r\n\r\nLet's take:\r\n\r\n![Mario](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/93594/36799057-22ead838-1ca4-11e8-8c6f-481e51438c82.gif)\r\n\r\nAnd take rectangle (126, 72, 16, 16) and output at 100x100.\r\n\r\nHere's the crop then resize:\r\n\r\n![Block](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/93594/36799307-bcac7b16-1ca4-11e8-9820-80055c5c7a23.png)\r\n\r\nWith resize then crop, we're increasing the size of the image by 6.25, so our rectangle becomes (787.5, 450, 100, 100). We have to either floor or round x, I'll go with floor:\r\n\r\n![Block with blurry edges](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/93594/36799609-7a0af2dc-1ca5-11e8-9ea6-e434a9f73202.png)\r\n\r\nIn this case, the blue is leaking in from the sides, despite the blue being cropped out (apart from the top left & right corner).\r\n\r\nThe used to be a problem with background position + background size, when using sprite sheets, but I believe browsers worked around it by cropping before resizing.\r\n\r\n**Edit:** The difference is subtle, so here's a zoom into the bottom-left corner:\r\n\r\n![corner1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/93594/36800033-7102315e-1ca6-11e8-82ed-251d41bf9f05.png) ![corner2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/93594/36800034-7119a9a6-1ca6-11e8-9ee1-8440eb4231b4.png)\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
